calls.reply:
The validator caught a real join error on the coach track: my cooldown hung off the *replicated* sprint step alone (`afterStep` + `instances:"all"`), and the runner resolved that reference 1,200 s early (6,600 s, the end of the block queue's second turn) instead of 7,800 s, so `debrief` collided with the last ten minutes of `time-sprints`. The fix keeps the physical constraint but removes the ambiguity: `cooldown-swim` now waits on a `compound "all"` of **the stopwatch stopping** (`time-sprints`, which ends the instant the last sprint is in — 7,800 s) **and** the block queue itself (the explicit three-turn barrier). Either way it resolves to 7,800 s, so cooldown runs 7,800–8,400 and debrief 8,400–9,000, with the coach's six steps strictly serial: 0–300, 300–1200, 1200–1260, 1500–1800, 6000–7800, 8400–9000. Makespan is exactly 9,000 s = 150 minutes of pool time, so every track finishes together on the ceiling the text sets.

